# Fingerprints (8 hex chars of sha256) of fake tokens that live in test fixtures.
# secret-leak-scan.py never reports these. One per line; text after # is a note.
# Only add a value you have confirmed is fake: a fingerprint silences every
# real appearance of the same string too.
#
# The fixture tokens in slack-automation pr-board/exercise_app.py (also in
# ci-kit/gh-read.test.cjs): repeated-character GitHub tokens, a Slack token
# shaped xoxb-1111-2222-..., and the AWS documentation example key.
dc920184  # GitHub token, one character repeated
86bab3b3  # GitHub token, one character repeated
046706a4  # Slack token, xoxb-1111-2222 shape
457643f4  # AWS access key, fixture value
# 8bcac790 (the "BEGIN PRIVATE KEY" header) is deliberately not listed: a real
# .pem file starts with the same header, so the fingerprint cannot tell them apart.
